# Kerr in Kerr's original ingoing coordinates `(v, r, θ, φ)`: full vacuum certificate

Data `In.gIn M a`, `In.giIn M a` (Visser E:K1), domain `domIn a = {Σ ≠ 0, sin θ ≠ 0}`, every real
`M`, `a`. The domain imposes no condition on `Δ`; `In.horizon_mem` exhibits points with `Δ = 0` in it
(for `0 < M`, `a² ≤ M²`). "Horizon" is used only as a name for the coordinate locus `Δ = 0`; no causal
or global statement is made. All fields are proved directly in these coordinates; nothing is
transported from Boyer–Lindquist.
-/

open scoped ContDiff

namespace ExactVacuumAtlas.Kerr.In

theorem ricci_flat (M a : ℝ) (x : Pt 4) (hx : x ∈ domIn a) (b d : Fin 4) :
    ricciOf (gIn M a) (giIn M a) b d x = 0 := by
  fin_cases b <;> fin_cases d
  exacts [ricci_0_0 M a x hx, ricci_0_1 M a x hx, ricci_0_2 M a x hx, ricci_0_3 M a x hx,
    ricci_1_0 M a x hx, ricci_1_1 M a x hx, ricci_1_2 M a x hx, ricci_1_3 M a x hx,
    ricci_2_0 M a x hx, ricci_2_1 M a x hx, ricci_2_2 M a x hx, ricci_2_3 M a x hx,
    ricci_3_0 M a x hx, ricci_3_1 M a x hx, ricci_3_2 M a x hx, ricci_3_3 M a x hx]

end ExactVacuumAtlas.Kerr.In

-- ==== solution ====
open scoped ContDiff
open ExactVacuumAtlas
open ExactVacuumAtlas.Kerr
open ExactVacuumAtlas.Kerr.In
theorem solution (M a : ℝ) : VacuumCertificate (gIn M a) (giIn M a) (domIn a) where
  isOpen := isOpen_domIn a
  nonempty := domIn_nonempty a
  symm x _ i j := symm M a x i j
  inv := inv M a
  smooth := smooth M a
  smooth_inv := smoothi M a
  lorentz := lorentz M a
  ricci_flat := ricci_flat M a
